::scene TITLE

ROOM studio_stage

EVENT FADE_IN

TITLE ferris_logo

::scene COMMERCIAL

CAM 1 STATIC

SHOT
A grey pistol on a grey table, shot flat and straight on. Nothing moves. There is no music. The camera does not push in, because nobody at Ferris has ever seen the point of that.
SHOT_END

NARRATOR:
The Ferris Model 9 service pistol.

6s

NARRATOR:
It does not jam.

4s

SHOT
The shot has not changed. The pistol has not moved. Somebody off-camera clears their throat.
SHOT_END

NARRATOR:
That is the advertisement.

CAM 2 STATIC

SHOT
The same pistol. The same table. A card is placed beside it by a hand in a plain sleeve, and withdrawn.
SHOT_END

OVERLAY
FERRIS

SAME DESIGN SINCE BEFORE THE HANDOFF

WE SAW NO REASON
OVERLAY_END

NARRATOR:
Ferris has never advertised, never changed the design, and never apologised for either.

NARRATOR:
If you require a handgun with a personality, our competitors will be delighted to sell you one.

3s

NARRATOR:
Theirs jam.

EVENT FADE_OUT

END
